---
import DocsLayout from '../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import { getPath } from '../../utils/paths';

const serdes = [
  { serde: 'StringSerde / I64Serde / BytesSerde', type: 'String / i64 / Bytes', feature: 'built in', use: 'Primitive keys and values.' },
  { serde: 'SchemaSerde<T, JsonSerde<T>>', type: 'any serde type that derives schemars::JsonSchema', feature: 'built in', use: 'Confluent JSON Schema.' },
  { serde: 'SchemaSerde<T, ProtobufSerde<T>>', type: 'a prost Message', feature: 'built in', use: 'Confluent Protobuf, resolved through prost-reflect.' },
  { serde: 'SchemaSerde<T, AvroSerde<T>>', type: 'apache_avro::AvroSchema', feature: 'built in', use: 'Confluent Avro.' },
  { serde: 'PolarsIpcSerde', type: 'polars::DataFrame', feature: 'polars', use: 'Columnar values as Arrow IPC.' },
  { serde: 'ArrowIpcSerde', type: 'arrow::RecordBatch', feature: 'arrow', use: 'Interchange with arrow-rs.' },
  { serde: 'ColumnarSerde<T>', type: 'columnar::Columnar', feature: 'columnar', use: 'Zero-copy native columnar values.' },
];

const models = [
  { model: 'Row model', api: 'Processor API and the high-level DSL', driver: 'TopologyTestDriver', note: 'Processes one record at a time. This is the model that matches Kafka Streams.' },
  { model: 'Columnar model', api: 'ColumnarTopology with Polars DataFrame edges', driver: 'ColumnarTestDriver', note: 'Vectorized aggregation over batches instead of single records.' },
];

const cargo = `[dependencies]
krabka-streams-rs = { version = "0.4", features = ["polars", "arrow"] }`;
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Serdes & Data Formats"
  description="Every serde krabka-streams-rs ships: Confluent Avro, Protobuf and JSON Schema through the registry, plus Arrow, Polars and native columnar values for vectorized work."
  currentSlug="/docs/data-formats"
>
  <div class="space-y-6">
    <div class="border-b border-white/10 pb-4">
      <h1 class="text-3xl font-extrabold text-white sm:text-4xl">Serdes & Data Formats</h1>
      <p class="text-gray-400 mt-2 text-base">
        Pick the encoding your topic carries, then hand it to the topology.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="space-y-4 text-sm text-gray-300 leading-relaxed">
      <p>
        A serde turns a Rust value into the bytes on a topic and back. The schema serdes resolve schema
        IDs against a Confluent-compatible registry and write the Confluent wire format, so a Java
        consumer reads what a Rust producer wrote. The columnar serdes are self-describing Arrow IPC
        and need no registry.
      </p>

      <div class="frosted-card rounded-xl overflow-hidden border border-white/10 not-prose">
        <table class="w-full text-left text-xs">
          <thead class="bg-slate-950/80 border-b border-white/10 uppercase text-gray-400 font-sans">
            <tr>
              <th class="py-3 px-4">Serde</th>
              <th class="py-3 px-4">Rust type</th>
              <th class="py-3 px-4">Cargo feature</th>
              <th class="py-3 px-4">Use it for</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody class="divide-y divide-white/5 font-sans">
            {serdes.map((s) => (
              <tr class="hover:bg-white/5 transition-colors">
                <td class="py-3 px-4 font-mono font-bold text-white text-xs">{s.serde}</td>
                <td class="py-3 px-4 font-mono text-gray-400 text-xs">{s.type}</td>
                <td class="py-3 px-4 font-mono text-krab-300 text-xs whitespace-nowrap">{s.feature}</td>
                <td class="py-3 px-4 text-gray-300">{s.use}</td>
              </tr>
            ))}
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white pt-2">Enable the ones you need</h2>

      <div class="not-prose bg-black/50 p-4 rounded-xl border border-white/5 relative font-mono text-xs">
        <div class="flex justify-between items-center text-gray-400 mb-2 font-sans">
          <span>Cargo.toml:</span>
          <button type="button" class="copy-btn flex items-center gap-1 rounded bg-white/5 px-2 py-1 text-gray-300 hover:bg-white/10 hover:text-white transition-all font-sans" data-copy={cargo}>
            <svg class="h-3.5 w-3.5" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M8 16H6a2 2 0 01-2-2V6a2 2 0 012-2h8a2 2 0 012 2v2m-6 12h8a2 2 0 002-2v-8a2 2 0 00-2-2h-8a2 2 0 00-2 2v8a2 2 0 002 2z" /></svg>
            <span>Copy</span>
          </button>
        </div>
        <pre class="text-krab-300 overflow-x-auto"><code>{cargo}</code></pre>
      </div>

      <p>
        The primitive and schema serdes are always available. The three columnar serdes each sit behind
        a Cargo feature, so a build that does not touch Arrow does not compile Arrow.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white pt-2">Two processing models</h2>

      <div class="frosted-card rounded-xl overflow-hidden border border-white/10 not-prose">
        <table class="w-full text-left text-xs">
          <thead class="bg-slate-950/80 border-b border-white/10 uppercase text-gray-400 font-sans">
            <tr>
              <th class="py-3 px-4">Model</th>
              <th class="py-3 px-4">Build it with</th>
              <th class="py-3 px-4">Test it with</th>
              <th class="py-3 px-4">Notes</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody class="divide-y divide-white/5 font-sans">
            {models.map((m) => (
              <tr class="hover:bg-white/5 transition-colors">
                <td class="py-3 px-4 font-bold text-white text-xs whitespace-nowrap">{m.model}</td>
                <td class="py-3 px-4 text-gray-300">{m.api}</td>
                <td class="py-3 px-4 font-mono text-krab-300 text-xs whitespace-nowrap">{m.driver}</td>
                <td class="py-3 px-4 text-gray-400">{m.note}</td>
              </tr>
            ))}
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <p>
        Both test drivers run a topology with no broker, so a unit test needs no cluster.
      </p>

      <p>
        The registry service that the schema serdes resolve against is documented on
        <a class="text-krab-400 hover:text-krab-300" href={getPath('/docs/schema-registry')}>Schema Registry &amp; Serdes</a>.
        The client and the topology API are on
        <a class="text-krab-400 hover:text-krab-300" href={getPath('/docs/streams-rs')}>Rust Streams &amp; Client</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</DocsLayout>
